y husband to handle  situations that he was handling and also  i just think it undermines and it's  disrespectful and that was definitely  something that i struggled with for a  while and being able to  have conversations with him on how much  that really bothered him  and just realizing how like not helpful  that was  was something that helped me to change  change that around and so now we kind of  have  a much more understanding of like hey  we're not going to be  parenting exactly the same every single  situation and i have learned a lot over  the years that it actually can be good  that you guys aren't going to be  parenting exactly the same  it's good that you're on like a similar  similar path it's common ground right  you don't really want opposite extremes  that's  that's not that's not going to be  helpful and that can cause a lot of  issues  but it's helpful to realize that like  hey maybe my partner is bringing  something else to the table that i  wouldn't have brought to the table  that i  might not have done in a certain way and  maybe i thought this wouldn't play out  well but seeing that it actually plays  out well for the way that dad's handling  it  and i think that like we bring different  energies to parenting  and we can't expect each other to be  exactly the same  if you if that's how you parent if both  you and your partner parent exactly the  same and you guys have the same  agreement on how to handle everything  then that's amazing go for that keep  doing that  but if you find yourself realizing that  like your partner's handling something  different than you would  i think it's helpful to just take a deep  breath  and realize it's okay and surrender and  let your partner handle it in a way  that's different than you would handle  it and have your partner's back and if  you really feel like a moment is  happening that you definitely don't  agree with like hey i definitely don't  think you should handle it that way  wait till after it's over wait till you  have a moment with your partner alone  without the kids around to have that  conversation and be like hey can we talk  about this  i'm not sure i think this  could have i think this could have been  handled differently what are your  thoughts on it  engage in like thoughtful discourse  where you're not like scolding your  partner or you're not like telling your  partner how it has to be or you did it  wrong  none of that i think it's much helpful  much more helpful to engage in  respectful discourse where you're saying  hey could we have possibly handled this  differently  what should we do different next time  and  if you find yourself getting into a  moment where you're getting heated or  overreacting can we have like a an  understanding or an agreement that like  the other person can step in like  because you might find your partner  you know overwhelmed and getting heated  and overreacting  and if you guys can come to an agreement  together to be like hey if i'm  overreacting how about like i you let me  step in and then you go take a breather  and vice versa if i'm getting  overwhelmed can we just like give each  other a look and you'll be like okay let  me come in and help tackle this in a  more respectful way because there's  times when  you know i have every intention to be my  most positive respectful self and to be  kind and handle it the way that i think  is optimal and then i find myself  getting more and more heated because i'm  in the moment  of chaos of all the kids having their  different things going on scouts like  spilling water everywhere you know  pouring it all out kovacs is crying at  my feet or i have him in the carrier and  he's crying and the other two are having  a sibling argument it can be very hard  to handle it the way that you have every  intention of handling it when you're  feeling tackled from all corners  so if your partner walks in and he's you  know just stepping in  to the moment hasn't been experiencing  it for a little bit  then if you have an agreement to be like  hey will you like  just tackle this for me this is what's  happening i need to step away and cool  down that's helpful for your kids to see  that you that when you feel yourself  heated that you're going to say hey i  need a couple moments to calm down and  then i'll come back because that teaches  them hey when i'm feeling upset before i  act in a way that's not healthy  or in a way that i don't mean to be that  i don't want to be maybe i can just take  a breather myself go walk away and  choose on my own to go walk away and  take a breather  so having communication with your  partner and saying this is what we're  going to do to have each other's back  and maybe we're not going to pair it  exactly the same but that's okay and  even good like that's one thing that i  had never even considered back when i  was first reading books on positive  parenting and um  and like attachment parenting and  respectful peaceful parenting i had  never read anywhere and i still haven't  really read  um what if your partner doesn't really  parent exactly like you  like maybe that's okay maybe that's good  actually at times that your partner is  gonna bring a different energy that  andrew brings a more masculine energy  that is still wonderful but handles  things in a different way that maybe i  would and maybe that's even good  sometimes but when it comes to a point  of  losing our cool if we can have an  agreement on how to handle it together  i think that creates a lot of peace in  the family where we have each other's  back we're not undermining each other  while one of us is parenting the other  and if you really disagree with  something that they've done like let's  talk about it a little later of course  this is not talking about extreme  situations of abuse or anything that is  not healthy like very like dangerous um  of course interject to your children and  this is a completely not the episode for  that and you know when it comes to abuse  i would love to discuss that with other  people in the podcast as well actually  in the future so just a little  clarification on that this does not  speak to every situation but we're  talking day to day with your partner  learning how to co-parent together in a  way that's symbiotic and peaceful and  just does really well  so i think that's like everything in my  notes that i wanted to talk about  ultimately  respect and unconditional love is like  the key to  to how to have a thriving relationship  and maybe it sounds vague like okay  respect unconditional love but how do i  do that but hopefully through  love languages showing each other love  learning how to parent together and  being respectful of each other's  differences even  can really help and go a long way and  trusting each other trust your partner  that they are doing their best too  and  they want to be spoken to in a way that  you want to be spoken to  so  working on yourself in that way because  if you work on yourself to  be the best version of yourself you're  going to have an easier time projecting  that out onto your children but also  your partner  when i'm not getting enough sleep now  i'm not getting like any kind of alone  fun time with girls like even if that if  that's like once every two weeks then i  can go have a few hours with some  friends  and just let my partner hang out with  the kids  even that helps replenish me a lot in  different in different ways so if i'm  able to take care of myself  and have basic basic necessities covered  of taking care of myself like a daily  shower and i know that there's like i've  seen memes online that are like hey a  shower is not a real break  for moms we need a real break and i i  agree i do think it's helpful and  important like i said to get some girl  time get some alone time go exercise by  yourself let your partner help take care  of you for that and if you're a single  mother maybe you're not listening to  this episode but if you are a single  parent  then obviously it's going to take  totally different adjustments and mad  props to anybody going that road in  regards to how  how much effort that is because i am  very thankful to be able to have my  husband there so that i can  let the kids hang out with him while i  go do something for myself for a couple  hours once in a while  but i do think that daily shower having  peace where i'm like hey don't let any  of the kids come in right now because  sometimes you know my younger one will  come in and take a little shower with me  and that's fine and beautiful and i love  that sometimes but sometimes i'm like  hey just like i'm gonna close the door  and just be alone in the shower just  take care of myself do some kind of like  mask or something that just like is  helpful for myself by myself for 20  minutes 30 minutes even and eating  healthy food you know all that all of  that i think is very helpful to be able  to be my most calm collected self so i'm  gonna act like my best self  so  i think that's everything for today i  hope that you found this video  or podcast of your listening helpful  and i hope you enjoyed it i love this  conversation of relationships and how to  thrive and how to parent and i  definitely want to delve into it more in  the future  with other people talking to them on the  podcast or even more by myself let me  know you liked it please leave a comment  and a review i would love that and  i will see you next time  [Music]
 

